course: dictionary
lesson: 8152
title: Require: need or must
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: To require something is to need it. «Many apps require users to be at least 13 years old.» The sentence tells you the apps need users to be 13 before they can use them, so require means need.
explain: Require can also mean that a rule makes something a must. «Being honest about what you did is always required.» Try swapping in need: «Being honest about what you did is always needed.» It still makes sense, so require means need here.
explain: Look for signs and forms. A box marked required must be filled in before you can send the form. Nobody is asking you nicely: the form needs the answer, and the rule says you must give it.
fact: Require means to need, or to make something a must.
fact: «A cake requires eggs» means a cake cannot be made without eggs.
fact: «Pupils are required to wear a uniform» means the school has a rule that they must.
fact: Living things require water, air and food to stay alive.
fact: In maths, «how many are required» asks how many of something are needed.
exercise: «Many apps require users to be at least 13 years old.» What does require mean here? | *Need or must have | Forget about | Make a noise about | Like very much
exercise: A plant requires water, air and light to grow. What does require mean? | *Needs | Ignores | Hides from | Shares
exercise: A pool sign says «Swimming hats required». What does required mean? | Lost property | *It is a rule, so you must wear one | You can choose if you like | Sold here
test: «Being honest about what you did is always required.» Which word could replace required without changing the meaning? | Forgotten | Hidden | Shared | *Needed
test: Ella's school form says: Name (required). What does required tell you? | It is about the weather | It is a nice picture | You may skip it if you like | *You must fill it in
exam: Which sentence shows require meaning a rule that makes something a must? | The dog ran fast. | We went to the park on Sunday. | *Pupils are required to wear a uniform. | The sun is bright today.
